\ An error raised inside a quotation body that made a definition leaves the transient lexical
\ frame open: the compiled epilogue's pop is skipped on an error return. The compiled-entry
\ boundary restores the depth instead.
\
\ The probe is the dictionary-shadow guard, which fires only when a definition lands in the import
\ frame. A stray frame left behind by the unwind would take the definition instead and the guard
\ would stay silent, so the throw below is what proves the depth came back.
\
\ There is no AOT redirect: a freeze executes the entry file's definition statements, so the last
\ line throws at build time rather than at binary runtime.

raiser: ( -- ) [ [ helper: ( -- n ) [ 1 ] ; f "boom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] call ] ;

[ raiser ] [ drop "caught" ] recover print-line

nip: ( -- y ) [ 0 ] ;
